# Public repository. The bulky but shareable parts ARE tracked: MP3/ and
# conf/playlist.txt. Live credentials and machine-local runtime state are not -
# the rules below say which, and why.

# The YouTube stream key. Anyone holding it can push to the channel. It was never
# committed; this rule makes that deliberate rather than merely accidental, so a future
# `git add -A` cannot sweep it in. conf/stream.env.example is the tracked template.
conf/stream.env
conf/stream.env.bak-*

# The external watchdog's config. Unlike stream.env this one holds a Gmail app password
# (the SMTP submission credential), so it must never be committed. The tracked template is
# conf/watchdog.env.example. The watchdog is the one component that runs OFF the streamer;
# see docs/watchdog.md.
conf/watchdog.env
conf/watchdog.env.bak-*

# OAuth refresh token for the Live Streaming API. Never committed - in a public repo most of
# all: it grants ongoing CONTROL of the channel, not just the ability to push pixels at it,
# and a refresh token in a public git history is a standing grant to anyone who finds it.
conf/yt_oauth.json

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from running the scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- runtime state: never track anything the running stream rewrites -----------------
# log/ and conf/golden.jpg are regenerated constantly (publisher.log is ffmpeg stderr,
# progress.txt is the frame counter, golden.jpg is re-grabbed at every publisher start).
# Both WERE tracked historically and their blobs are still in the public git history; these
# rules only stop new copies. Removing the old ones would need a history rewrite and a
# force-push, a separate and deliberate decision. Do not blame the 353 MB .git on them,
# though: measured across all of history log/ is 26.6 MB and conf/ is 3.7 MB, while the
# tracked MP3/ library is 328.4 MB of it. The weight is the music, not the logs.
# They are machine-local state, not source.
log/
conf/golden.jpg

# Test-suite scratch. tests/lib.sh gives every case its own tree under here and removes it
# again, but an interrupted run can leave one behind - never commit it.
tests/.tmp/

# Release build scratch: release.sh exports the tagged tree here, packs it and deletes it.
# An interrupted release can leave one behind; never commit it.
.release-build/

# Editor/tool backups of the scripts. Git IS the backup.
bin/*.bak-*
conf/*.bak-*
